WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.838
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:09.640
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:17.330
Unit thirty-six: Ability in the Past. Today you will distinguish general ability from one specific success.

4
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.340
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.498
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.177
Could.

7
00:00:27.183 --> 00:00:29.740
Could means general ability in the past.

8
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:31.815
I could swim at five.

9
00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:35.382
Your turn. Say: Could.

10
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:39.025
Could.

11
00:00:39.783 --> 00:00:40.854
Was able to.

12
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.279
Was able to means ability on one occasion.

13
00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:46.279
I was able to finish.

14
00:00:46.883 --> 00:00:49.559
Your turn. Say: Was able to.

15
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.610
Was able to.

16
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.386
Managed to.

17
00:00:56.383 --> 00:00:58.859
Managed to means succeeded with difficulty.

18
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:00.881
I managed to open it.

19
00:01:01.483 --> 00:01:04.031
Your turn. Say: Managed to.

20
00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:07.810
Managed to.

21
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.621
Succeeded in.

22
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:12.651
Succeeded in means achieved a goal.

23
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.052
She succeeded in passing.

24
00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.360
Your turn. Say: Succeeded in.

25
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.549
Succeeded in.

26
00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.029
Couldn't.

27
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.063
Couldn't means unable in the past.

28
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:28.790
I couldn't come.

29
00:01:29.383 --> 00:01:31.827
Your turn. Say: Couldn't.

30
00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:35.470
Couldn't.

31
00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:37.554
General ability.

32
00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.478
General ability means something you could always do.

33
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:43.340
General ability.

34
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.823
Your turn. Say: General ability.

35
00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.155
General ability.

36
00:01:51.917 --> 00:01:53.359
Specific occasion.

37
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:57.151
Specific occasion means one particular time.

38
00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.320
A specific occasion.

39
00:01:59.917 --> 00:02:03.231
Your turn. Say: Specific occasion.

40
00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.497
Specific occasion.

41
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.263
Achievement.

42
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.876
Achievement means something successfully done.

43
00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:14.728
A great achievement.

44
00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:17.899
Your turn. Say: Achievement.

45
00:02:20.733 --> 00:02:21.711
Achievement.

46
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.070
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:30.542
Visal, write one sentence with could and one with managed to.

48
00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:44.057
When I was five, I could swim. Yesterday, I managed to finish the whole report. Could is for general ability, and managed to is for one specific success.

49
00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.592
What is the difference?

50
00:02:47.683 --> 00:03:03.263
General ability: I could read at four. One specific occasion: I was able to, managed to or succeeded in. The fire was big, but everyone was able to escape. We do not say everyone could escape in this meaning.

51
00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.699
What about negatives?

52
00:03:06.783 --> 00:03:22.026
Couldn't works for both: I couldn't swim, and I couldn't finish the test. Managed to suggests difficulty. Succeeded in is followed by -ing: She succeeded in passing the exam. All of these show an achievement.

53
00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:24.737
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:31.542
Grammar focus: Past ability: could, was able to, managed to, succeeded in.

55
00:03:31.842 --> 00:03:32.959
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.417
When I was five, I could swim.

57
00:03:36.317 --> 00:03:39.082
Yesterday I managed to finish the whole report.

58
00:03:39.983 --> 00:03:42.111
She succeeded in passing the exam.

59
00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:50.749
Could = general past ability. Was able to / managed to / succeeded in = one specific success. Couldn't = both.

60
00:03:51.483 --> 00:03:55.111
Be careful! Don't say: I could finish it yesterday.

61
00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.682
Say: I managed to finish it yesterday.

62
00:03:59.982 --> 00:04:01.331
Use managed to.

63
00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:05.111
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.029
What Could You Do?.

65
00:04:07.329 --> 00:04:09.677
When I was five, I could swim quite well.

66
00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:13.398
Yesterday I managed to finish the whole report.

67
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.212
The fire was big, but everyone was able to escape.

68
00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.198
She succeeded in passing the exam on her first try.

69
00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.840
This was a real achievement.

70
00:04:24.933 --> 00:04:28.900
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.504
When I was a child, I blank climb trees.

72
00:04:32.804 --> 00:04:36.922
A, could. B, managed. C, succeeded.

73
00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:42.130
The answer is A: could.

74
00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.434
After hours of work, I blank finish it.

75
00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:49.457
A, could. B, managed to. C, succeed.

76
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.278
The answer is B: managed to.

77
00:04:56.417 --> 00:04:58.219
She succeeded blank passing.

78
00:04:58.519 --> 00:05:01.267
A, in. B, to. C, at.

79
00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:06.763
The answer is A: in.

80
00:05:07.917 --> 00:05:09.417
Which shows difficulty?

81
00:05:09.717 --> 00:05:13.254
A, managed to. B, could. C, couldn't.

82
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.649
The answer is A: managed to.

83
00:05:19.783 --> 00:05:22.410
According to the reading, who escaped the fire?

84
00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:26.131
A, everyone. B, nobody. C, the dog.

85
00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:31.318
The answer is A: everyone.

86
00:05:32.533 --> 00:05:35.731
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:39.570
Write one sentence with 'could' and one with 'managed to'.

88
00:05:48.383 --> 00:05:49.791
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:50.091 --> 00:06:03.125
When I was young, I could run very fast. Yesterday I managed to finish a difficult exercise after two hours. I use could for general ability and managed to for one achievement.

90
00:06:03.425 --> 00:06:05.018
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:05.917 --> 00:06:12.470
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past ability: could, was able to, managed to, succeeded in.

92
00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:17.024
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

93
00:06:17.324 --> 00:06:20.836
See you in Unit thirty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:21.136 --> 00:06:24.148
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

